<title>UK: Kingfisher up on quarterly sales figures.</title>
<headline>Kingfisher up on quarterly sales figures.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Kingfisher Plc rose to near its 1997 high on Wednesday, after the retailer announced robust quarterly sales figures.</p>
<p>Kingfisher was up 5p to 725p by 0825 GMT, after touching a intraday high of 733p in the opening minutes of trade.</p>
<p>&quot;Sales were better than expected and pushed the stock&quot;, a trader said.</p>
<p>Kingfisher said retail sales in the 13 weeks ended May 3 rose by 8.0 percent on a like-for-like basis and by 10.1 percent overall.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
